## Pass/Fail Criteria

**PASS:**
- Connection to database succeeds
- All tables have rows > 0
- All vCMTS tables have data within the last 5 minutes
- All CM tables have data within the last 5 minutes
- SFID mapping returns valid us/ds service flow names
- Latency, AQM, congestion, and sanctioned tables show data per modem
- Polling intervals are consistent (~15-30 seconds)

**FAIL:**
- Connection fails
- Any table has 0 rows
- Any table has stale data (vCMTS > 5 min, CM > 24 hours)
- SFID mapping returns no results for a registered modem
- Polling intervals show large gaps (> 2 minutes)

## Notes
- Replace `0c:b9:37:64:3a:b0` with your actual cable modem MAC (colon-separated lowercase)
- Use Alt+P / Alt+N in IDLE to scroll through previous commands
- The `run()` helper function prints results in a table format — define it once and reuse
- Step 17 is the quickest health check — paste the whole block for an instant summary
- `conn.close()` when done to clean up the connection